{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099918-for-a-technomancer-is-there-any-reason-ever-not-to-use-wonder-spheres","id":1099918,"title":"For a Technomancer is there any reason ever not to use wonder spheres?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-03T14:33:03-07:00","id":1099918,"title":"For a Technomancer is there any reason ever not to use wonder spheres?","content":"I mean, combined with the rules for Devices in Technomancers Toybox, you're spending half XP on spheres for the sole drawback of 'only' being able to use them to create gizmos. Gizmos that themselves are far more powerful than any improvised effect ever could be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T14:50:31-07:00","id":1099925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099918-for-a-technomancer-is-there-any-reason-ever-not-to-use-wonder-spheres#post1099918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, combined with the rules for Devices in Technomancers Toybox, you're spending half XP on spheres for the sole drawback of 'only' being able to use them to create gizmos. Gizmos that themselves are far more powerful than any improvised effect ever could be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Look at M20 p.653. All wonders cost XP to craft, without exception. On top of this you'll be starting with zero spells and will be highly limited in your ability to get more spells, as creating a wonder is a lengthy process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T16:37:52-07:00","id":1099947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099918-for-a-technomancer-is-there-any-reason-ever-not-to-use-wonder-spheres#post1099918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, combined with the rules for Devices in Technomancers Toybox, you're spending half XP on spheres for the sole drawback of 'only' being able to use them to create gizmos. Gizmos that themselves are far more powerful than any improvised effect ever could be.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Gizmos are one particular effect. a matter 2 one would allow you to melt things which is useful but someone with matter 2 can melt things, freeze things transmute one thing into another. you lose serious amounts of versatility.<br /> <br /> <br /> You're basically a D&amp;D wizard who can invent spells more quickly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T16:51:51-07:00","id":1099952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099918-for-a-technomancer-is-there-any-reason-ever-not-to-use-wonder-spheres?p=1099947#post1099947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Gizmos are one particular effect. a matter 2 one would allow you to melt things which is useful but someone with matter 2 can melt things, freeze things transmute one thing into another. you lose serious amounts of versatility.<br /> <br /> <br /> You're basically a D&amp;D wizard who can invent spells more quickly</div> </div> </div> </div>And who has considerably more spell components, without the option of using an Arcane Focus instead. Which, for a Technomancer, would be the kind of Instruments they could employ with full Sphere levels. And their spell components could be huge and unwieldy, depending on your character's particular methodology. Potentially, you're limited to how many different Wonders you can carry at any given time.<br /> <br /> Using the Wonder Spheres, you wouldn't be able to have a Virtual Adept who uses their laptop or arm-mounted keyboard for a bunch of things. Nor could your Etherite go full Doctor Who and break out a sonic screwdriver. Every time you wanted to cast a new Effect - or even a variant on an existing one - you'd need to go to the lab.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T17:00:17-07:00","id":1099956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099918-for-a-technomancer-is-there-any-reason-ever-not-to-use-wonder-spheres?p=1099925#post1099925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes. Look at M20 p.653. All wonders cost XP to craft, without exception.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but that's M20, an edition that, thus far, hasn't covered the Wonder Sphere variant rules at all. You have to go back to Sons of Ether Revised before you get Wonder Spheres.<br /> <br /> Since M20 has nothing to say about Wonder Spheres or Gizmos, I caution against applying the XP requirement as-is. More likely, we'd treat Gizmos as Unique Instruments, usable only by an Enlightened character whose Focus accepts the Gizmo's underlying concept. It isn't even really an Artifact, since you still need the required Sphere levels to use it (whereas an Artifact has the Effect built in).<br /> <br /> But I'm just spit-balling suggestions. While I still don't think M20's rules directly apply here, I'm not committed to the above interpretation on how one WOULD run them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T19:02:47-07:00","id":1099979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099918-for-a-technomancer-is-there-any-reason-ever-not-to-use-wonder-spheres?p=1099952#post1099952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And who has considerably more spell components, without the option of using an Arcane Focus instead. Which, for a Technomancer, would be the kind of Instruments they could employ with full Sphere levels. And their spell components could be huge and unwieldy, depending on your character's particular methodology. Potentially, you're limited to how many different Wonders you can carry at any given time.<br /> <br /> Using the Wonder Spheres, you wouldn't be able to have a Virtual Adept who uses their laptop or arm-mounted keyboard for a bunch of things. Nor could your Etherite go full Doctor Who and break out a sonic screwdriver. Every time you wanted to cast a new Effect - or even a variant on an existing one - you'd need to go to the lab.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You'd have an item for each spell and can't make new ones but you could &quot;prepare a bunch&quot; in advance. its an interesting character but clearly has downsides.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T22:26:44-07:00","id":1100015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099918-for-a-technomancer-is-there-any-reason-ever-not-to-use-wonder-spheres?p=1099952#post1099952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And who has considerably more spell components, without the option of using an Arcane Focus instead. Which, for a Technomancer, would be the kind of Instruments they could employ with full Sphere levels. And their spell components could be huge and unwieldy, depending on your character's particular methodology. Potentially, you're limited to how many different Wonders you can carry at any given time.<br /> <br /> Using the Wonder Spheres, you wouldn't be able to have a Virtual Adept who uses their laptop or arm-mounted keyboard for a bunch of things. Nor could your Etherite go full Doctor Who and break out a sonic screwdriver. Every time you wanted to cast a new Effect - or even a variant on an existing one - you'd need to go to the lab.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except of course you CAN build multipurpose wonders. So any effect you can think of you can have. Yeah, you don't get to do just ANYTHING. But...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T23:56:45-07:00","id":1100028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099918-for-a-technomancer-is-there-any-reason-ever-not-to-use-wonder-spheres?p=1100015#post1100015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except of course you CAN build multipurpose wonders. So any effect you can think of you can have. Yeah, you don't get to do just ANYTHING. But...</div> </div> </div> </div>No you can't. You can add onto a wonder but you cannot have the full versatility of a sphere in a single device. You have to set up all the effects your character can do ahead of time. And you need a steady access to appropriate Tass if you want to be able to anything as a Starting character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T04:20:43-07:00","id":1100067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099918-for-a-technomancer-is-there-any-reason-ever-not-to-use-wonder-spheres?p=1100028#post1100028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No you can't. You can add onto a wonder but you cannot have the full versatility of a sphere in a single device. You have to set up all the effects your character can do ahead of time. And you need a steady access to appropriate Tass if you want to be able to anything as a Starting character.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, exactly.<br /> <br /> If a technomancer using only Wonder Spheres created an energy weapon, for example, they could add any number of distinct functions to it. One function turns it into a heat ray, another into a freeze ray, still another into a disintegration ray. But those would be three Effects, painstakingly added in the lab. And they'd be the ONLY three Effects the technomancer could use the weapon for. They wouldn't be able to tweak the gun with an understanding of Time to make the freeze function work for cryogenics. Nor could they alter settings on the fly to make the beams affect spirits. And if the technomancer wanted to use the heat ray function to warm up a can of soup, they'd just destroy the can (because, obviously, there's only one heat setting on the gun: lethal heat, meant as an attack).<br /> <br /> Taking the Wonder Sphere option represents a Player sacrificing flexibility for lower XP costs. But if your character can only ever create Wonders, they are only a step or two removed from being an unAwakened Sorcerer, who goes to great lengths to acquire even the simplest of powers. That is the cost inherent in the exchange.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T12:30:17-07:00","id":1100189,"title":"","content":"Actually, you totally can. Perhaps not lore-wise. But you can totally go through and take every codified effect of a sphere level and put in a function for that in a device. It's not even hard to do because versatility isn't something they valued highly in the costs of making wonders.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, you're using sphere effects twice as high as your compatriots who purchase traditional spheres, and are getting themselves blown up by paradox by quick-casting. You're purchasing the 'privilege' of using THE SINGLE MOST likely to get you slapped by paradox way to use magic in the game. Meanwhile, the wonder sphere users' main drawback is a need for tass/quintessence. Which isn't hard to get.<br /> <br /> As to your heat ray analogy. <i>You can build wonders to do litterally anything magic could do.</i> You have to plan ahead, yes. But you don't have to go &quot;I've got a heat ray that has one setting.&quot; you could go &quot;I have a device that controls heat.&quot; Your only limitation is you have to come up with a guiding theory for how the device works. Is it really that hard to say &quot;It emits phlogiston rays generated by a rare earth magnet in contact with the legendary metal orichalcum. A dial on the side controls just how close to the metal the magnet is and thereby the level of heat that is emitted.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hell, even space constraints aren't a thing once you get Correspondence 4. You just create pocket dimensions inside your devices to contain all the inner workings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T13:46:29-07:00","id":1100205,"title":"","content":"Erm. No, you can't do that. Artifacts hold rotes, not general descriptions of rotes.<br /> <br /> Unlike Spheres, Rotes/Procedures have rules. If you design your ray to cause damage, it needs damage rules. A &quot;control heat&quot; ray would have to specify how it works, including things like range, duration, area of effect, and how the power of the effect it's distributed (all of these things require successes).<br /> <br /> Since you want to weaponize it, you need to think how many successes you need to produce a lethal a mount of heat/cold (it will need more successes the more heat displaced, as usual). It won't be 2 lethal per success because you need to past the treshold of heating your cofee. Unless you want the ray to have two &quot;modes&quot; with different rules...but then it would have two effects (Same sphere, same level, different ruleset. Sounds like two rotes to me)<br /> <br /> Also, one will have to meditate on the effect of concentrating all the heat of a place on a person. As toaster... if you don't mind cooling the room to cook your bread it may be ok. But to kill a guy instantaneously you will probably have to drop local temperature to less that nice (if that's even possible within your specifications). On the other hand, if you're in a very cold place, you could freeze someone and get a nice puff of heat<br /> <br /> As a laser torch it's a failure, because it can't work under cold environments. As a freezing ray, it's likely harder to work under heat because you need to remove more heat to start causing damage (not very impresive)<br /> <br /> Since you lack specification, you think that everything can be done, but this isn't true because you will need to specify every detail, every rule, of the artifact. And you won't be able to duplicate every effect you need.<br /> <br /> &quot;Why would I buy Matter to destroy matter when I can just bring my plasma gun?&quot;...sometimes Matter will just work better","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-04-2017, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T17:22:29-07:00","id":1100273,"title":"","content":"That's the thing. There's nothing stopping you from building in general effects for general purposes. Then specific effects for specific purposes. And devices only need 1 success. Ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T17:54:27-07:00","id":1100279,"title":"","content":"As with all Mage rule discussions, it ends with &quot;see if you can get your ST to agree with it.&quot; I personally wouldn't allow a tricorder whose described functions are, &quot;everything that Life 4 allows.&quot; The point of Wonder Spheres in the first place is to trade versatility for raw power. But I'm not your ST so who cares? As for what's in the book, well, Mage rules have so many loopholes they're basically Swiss cheese already, but that doesn't mean anyone's bound to leave those holes intact in their games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T06:30:17-07:00","id":1100423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099918-for-a-technomancer-is-there-any-reason-ever-not-to-use-wonder-spheres?p=1100273#post1100273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the thing. There's nothing stopping you from building in general effects for general purposes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you name 1 artifact in all of mage that achieve to encompass everything that a single sphere dot can do?<br /> Can you name (or invent, <i>but within the rules, that is, with a system</i>) a Rote or combination of Rotes that can encompass what a single Sphere Level can do?<br /> <br /> I highly doubt it. But go and prove me wrong.<br /> <br /> Unless you do, you will have a Mage that hasn't the versatility of a Sphere at hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T06:58:51-07:00","id":1100430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099918-for-a-technomancer-is-there-any-reason-ever-not-to-use-wonder-spheres?p=1100423#post1100423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Can you name 1 artifact in all of mage that achieve to encompass everything that a single sphere dot can do?<br /> Can you name (or invent, <i>but within the rules, that is, with a system</i>) a Rote or combination of Rotes that can encompass what a single Sphere Level can do?<br /> <br /> I highly doubt it. But go and prove me wrong.<br /> <br /> Unless you do, you will have a Mage that hasn't the versatility of a Sphere at hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>To expand further, making Artifacts at all is an involved process. It's why a vast majority of them are single-Effect items. It would take forever to add enough Rotes to an artifact that is functioned nearly identically to a Sphere or even Sphere level. A character whose entire technomagickal ability comes from the Wonders they craft is better served creating a bunch of specialized ones, then making due with them, than trying to make a single Artifact do everything.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, there's a very good reason to create a bunch of different Wonders, rather than all in one: if that one Wonder is stolen/broken/destroyed/becomes tainted by evil, you lose a huge chunk of your magick. Setting aside the huge investment in time and resources now wasted, it's putting all your eggs in one basket. The Revised Storyteller Companion made the good point that while you could make an Artifact Talisman Unique Instrument Periapt that is also a Familiar and Mentor, all in one item, you probably shouldn't.<br /> <br /> All of this assuming, of course, that it's even sensible for a single Artifact to do everything a Sphere can do, or what a single Sphere level can do in some cases (Time 3 is doable, Forces 3 less so). Especially for technomagickal machines, there's conceptually only so much you can make the Artifact do by default. The scientist's very Focus may - and probably does - limit how many different functions can be crammed into one package, and still be expected to function.<br /> <br /> A Storyteller is fully within their rights to ask a player whether cramming a million Rotes into a single Artifact is even possible under their character's worldview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T07:09:33-07:00","id":1100433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And devices only need 1 success. Ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I forgot: No, Devices don't work like this. Check any plasma cannon, any laser gun, you will see that you need more than one success for any device with a scalable (or damage) effect.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T14:48:13-07:00","id":1100594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099918-for-a-technomancer-is-there-any-reason-ever-not-to-use-wonder-spheres?p=1100273#post1100273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the thing. There's nothing stopping you from building in general effects for general purposes. Then specific effects for specific purposes. And devices only need 1 success. Ever.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Except having to make each effect individually. You can't have &quot;does everything forces 1 does&quot; You'd have a setting for &quot;Infrared sight&quot; and one for &quot;electric sight&quot; (These would be two separate builds) low light vision(third build). So while you could keep adding powers to your amazing Sonic Screwdriver. Your character has to spend more time and effort working on these things than your average mage. Is less capable broadly AND if you lose your WOnder you're SOL. And you don't even get the bonus for Unique Focus.<br /> <br /> Its not an unreasonable build with alot of advantages(and for all it showing up in SOE Its probably Technocratically far more common!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T16:24:24-07:00","id":1100637,"title":"","content":"There's nothing that actually contradicts devices working like that? Litterally anywhere.<br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022 Cascade 23 Laser Pistol<br /> Arete 4, Primal Energy 20, Background Cost 6<br /> Among the most common of the energy weapons employed<br /> by the Union, the Cascade 23 is compact, light and<br /> deadly. Powered by a converter that strips Primal Energy into<br /> a more usable form (and thus avoids the problems of molecular<br /> bonding energy limits), it is capable of several shots with a<br /> good deal of punch. Unfortunately, it\u2019s still not completely<br /> accepted by the Masses, and it\u2019s prone to failure on Earth.<br /> Doubtless due to unsanitary conditions, gravity, jostling and<br /> so forth, of course!<br /> The Cascade 23 uses its Arete rating to fire a Forces blast<br /> as a laser, costing one point of Primal Energy per shot. Though<br /> it doesn\u2019t really do that much damage, it\u2019s a handy hold-out<br /> energy weapon, especially in space where it\u2019s not subject to<br /> failure. Botches with the weapon tend to result in meltdowns,<br /> electrical power pack discharges and similar mishaps.<br /> <br /> It simply specifies that it uses it's arete rating. Which could go either way. If we take the fluff as indicative of it's power, it would be more accurate to the fluff of the thing to say it simply does one success worth of damage. Because if we go with Arete 4 as the limit of it's potential stopping power. That translates to a 2-9 dice of lethal damage. More than enough to hospitalize or immolate a sleeper in a single shot. Hardly something that 'is a handy hold out weapon that doesn't do that much damage'<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 NSN Plasma Caster<br /> Arete 6, Primal Energy 30, Background Cost 10<br /> The true heavy weapon of the Void Engineer Marine arsenal,<br /> this device (which is almost never used on Earth) fires a bolt<br /> of superheated plasma that incinerates nearly anything. Obviously,<br /> its functions are highly vulgar and subject to some pretty<br /> terrible backlashes, like melting the user. When it hits, though,<br /> there\u2019s little that can stand in its way. The NSN Plasma Caster<br /> resembles a large rifle-like weapon with a stabilizing handle and<br /> a multi-pronged induction chamber on the end of the barrel; it\u2019s<br /> usually painted dark blue, dark green or gray.<br /> The NSN inflicts regular Forces damage, which is aggravated,<br /> to boot. Wielders use the Skill: Energy Weapons;<br /> additionally, since it\u2019s so heavy and encumbering, the user<br /> should have a Strength of at least 3 \u2014 each dot less imposes<br /> a one-die firing penalty.<br /> <br /> And this one is even WORSE as it doesn't tell you anything at all! Even how much PE each shot costs! There's a reason why I tend towards using energy weapons I design. Out of the Three energy weapons in the Guide to the Technocracy, the only one that conforms to the way you believe it should work, is the Cyborg Plasma Cannon Implant.<br /> <br /> Two, since you can buy your way up to prime 4 faster, you can build wonders which bind themselves to your pattern a-la cybernetics or the ruby slippers faster. Meaning to take your toys they have to cut them out of/off of you.<br /> <br /> Finally why would you need to detect each little thing seperately? Rather than just building a 'quantify energy' rote into the machine.<br /> <br /> And while yes, you do have to spend time designing and building these things, there's no reason you should do that by hand. It's openly stated in the Technomancers Toybox that the only thing stopping any particular SoE and the VA from setting up mass production facilities is personal taste. And that the Technocracy actually DOES have assembly lines that churn out plasma cannons. Which given the quickening is a vulgar prime effect.... Is there anything stopping you from simply building a device that performs the quickening? This all requires monstrous amounts of Tass. But Tass is hardly hard to come by for the determined mage.<br /> <br /> And the kicker is, devices allow you to <i>share power with allies.</i> Which is a total gamechanger. An Etherite with his cult with dozens of followers on Ether-cycles flying through the sky, firing off death rays and using their chronotron goggles to see alternate futures and thus dodge lasers from a technocrat convoy below.... is a lot scarier than one Hermetic who's as liable to blow himself up as he is the enemy because there are sleepers in that convoy. Is the power unlimited? no. There are definitely limits to how far one can push the consensus via artifacts and devices. But in the end... one takes time and resources. That's the downside. Because quick-casting sucks. And you can put rotes into wonders. And there are only so many rotes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T16:49:39-07:00","id":1100646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099918-for-a-technomancer-is-there-any-reason-ever-not-to-use-wonder-spheres?p=1100637#post1100637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Finally why would you need to detect each little thing seperately? Rather than just building a 'quantify energy' rote into the machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because you can't? You seem to think &quot;Forces 1&quot; is a rote. Its not &quot;Low light vision&quot; is a rote. Every power you want to have in a device. You have to name in detail every power you want the device to have. Have to build many of them seprately and NO you can't apply the design for your &quot;electrcity manipulator&quot; to your &quot;heat manipulator&quot; each is designed seperately.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And while yes, you do have to spend time designing and building these things, there's no reason you should do that by hand. It's openly stated in the Technomancers Toybox that the only thing stopping any particular SoE and the VA from setting up mass production facilities is personal taste. </div> </div> </div>And Syndicate Rev shows how easy it is to do so. Its both extremely time consuming and not &quot;I press a button instant wonder&quot;. IF the wonder is new you take a while to design it. Even a previous design still takes the active management of enlightened personel.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that the Technocracy actually DOES have assembly lines that churn out plasma cannons. </div> </div> </div>Yes the Technocracy has the resources(including having low level interns) to be able to mass produce plasma cannons. Said Mass production would not include, Ice cannons, Plasma pistols, Sonic screw drivers etc. Each of course could be mass produced but each requires both signficant resources AND a separate setup.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which given the quickening is a vulgar prime effect.... Is there anything stopping you from simply building a device that performs the quickening? This all requires monstrous amounts of Tass. But Tass is hardly hard to come by for the determined mage. </div> </div> </div>Tass is a bitch to get, because you need stuff that's appropriate for it. You'd need multiple level 5 nodes which you know is why the Technocracy is able to pull it off.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the kicker is, devices allow you to <i>share power with allies.</i> Which is a total gamechanger. An Etherite with his cult with dozens of followers on Ether-cycles flying through the sky, firing off death rays and using their chronotron goggles to see alternate futures and thus dodge lasers from a technocrat convoy below.... is a lot scarier than one Hermetic who's as liable to blow himself up as he is the enemy because there are sleepers in that convoy. Is the power unlimited? no. There are definitely limits to how far one can push the consensus via artifacts and devices. But in the end... one takes time and resources. That's the downside. Because quick-casting sucks. And you can put rotes into wonders. And there are only so many rotes. </div> </div> </div>technocracy pulls out EMP all the Etherites crash and die. Your wonder stops working and you have no powers. Meanwhile said hermetic who has spent as much time as you have building wonders and making your cult making spirit pacts with Angels so the pop out of the umbra and murder the technos.. its vulgar as hell but SPirits don't take paradox.<br /> <br /> Wonder spheres give an xp advantage. They Don't give you Free Resources Anyone who has the same amount of tass and time can do equally crazy shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T18:08:02-07:00","id":1100664,"title":"","content":"Err no. Low Light vision is not a rote. QUANTIFY FORCES. Is a rote. I'm not pulling that out of my ass. It's literally right there in the book as the only level 1 forces rote. And it explicitly detects every kind of energy including kinetic energy in the area it's used on. To a mage, electricity and heat are just two seperate aspects of a universal energy.<br /> <br /> Err no. It's slightly time consuming. You build the production facility which is a wonder in it's own right, admittedly requiring some setup time. And then it really is insert tass, push button, get wonder. Again, if you look at the rules for wonder creation and wonder use, this is how they interact. The primary limit is how much tass you can obtain and the actual mundane crafting of the shells. The quickening itself is ludicrously trivial with the aid of wonders.<br /> <br /> At the levels of prime we're talking, the resonance of a particular batch of tass is irrelevant. You break tass of the wrong resonance down into free quintessence. Then remake it in whichever form is required. Prime 4 allows the creation of tass using quintessence.<br /> <br /> Literally, how the heck would an EMP stop something that doesn't work on electrical principles? You could try and countermagick it, and that would certainly be attempted. But they would have to countermagick each and every individual wonder. You're correct in saying they don't give you free resources, but spheres can GET you resources. the time the hermetic would require to hunt down tass of the appropriate type is sidestepped by machines that simply remake it. Sources of quintessence can be made. Whether as simple as drawing electricity from the power grid into a capacitor and breaking it down into quintessence and then converting it into tass for use in machining new devices. Or as complex as creating a wonder with an internal periapt that uses the font of heaven rote to fill itself with quintessence, before dumping that quintessence into the stores of a nearby manufacturing wonder.<br /> <br /> Spheres grant options for gaining resources. Therefor something that let's you grab those sphere levels faster DOES in fact grant you more resources.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T21:12:12-07:00","id":1100694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099918-for-a-technomancer-is-there-any-reason-ever-not-to-use-wonder-spheres?p=1100664#post1100664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Err no. Low Light vision is not a rote. QUANTIFY FORCES. Is a rote. I'm not pulling that out of my ass. It's literally right there in the book as the only level 1 forces rote. And it explicitly detects every kind of energy including kinetic energy in the area it's used on. To a mage, electricity and heat are just two seperate aspects of a universal energy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just no? Burn out is a Rote. Manipulate Forces is not. I'll point out Matter which also has Matter perceptions as its normal descriptor taht doesn't mean Fragment of the Dream isn't the rote.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Err no. It's slightly time consuming. You build the production facility which is a wonder in it's own right, admittedly requiring some setup time. And then it really is insert tass, push button, get wonder. Again, if you look at the rules for wonder creation and wonder use, this is how they interact. The primary limit is how much tass you can obtain and the actual mundane crafting of the shells. The quickening itself is ludicrously trivial with the aid of wonders. </div> </div> </div>IF you don't think &quot;Build a whole damn factory so I can do this&quot; isn't a serious time consuming endevour while another mage who isn't building a whole damned factory they do other things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At the levels of prime we're talking, the resonance of a particular batch of tass is irrelevant. You break tass of the wrong resonance down into free quintessence. Then remake it in whichever form is required. Prime 4 allows the creation of tass using quintessence. </div> </div> </div>Its not just resonence but yes you could make a prime 4 Matter 4 one for cleaning up Tass for use for any wonder you can possibly experience.. this is of course completely beyond a starting level character.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Literally, how the heck would an EMP stop something that doesn't work on electrical principles? </div> </div> </div>Your advanced flying technology has no electronic parts? Then I'm calling it vulgar.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But they would have to countermagick each and every individual wonder. You're correct in saying they don't give you free resources, but spheres can GET you resources. the time the hermetic would require to hunt down tass of the appropriate type is sidestepped by machines that simply remake it. </div> </div> </div>And the time it took you to make and design that machine he was doing other things. The hermetic who isn't making wonders may not actually care. Or he gets approrpirate tass and makes angel Fetishes. I guess you could make a Fetish assembly line but I think that's where you get attacked by so many things.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sources of quintessence can be made. Whether as simple as drawing electricity from the power grid into a capacitor and breaking it down into quintessence and then converting it into tass for use in machining new devices. Or as complex as creating a wonder with an internal periapt that uses the font of heaven rote to fill itself with quintessence, before dumping that quintessence into the stores of a nearby manufacturing wonder. </div> </div> </div><br /> I think you've come at this from the perspective of &quot;I'm a master of all spheres to start because its cheaper&quot; rather than a starting character working twoards these things since you consistantly throw out high level sphere effects and infinite resources.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is so completely in white roomland.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spheres grant options for gaining resources. Therefor something that let's you grab those sphere levels faster DOES in fact grant you more resources. </div> </div> </div>It takes Just as long to learn a wondersphere as it does a true sphere. It has the same learning time. It just says you can buy it for half cost. So you can spend time learning other things!<br /> <br /> Also you can't start with 12 wonder spheres you start with 6 standard spheres and can start buying wonder spheres with freebies at 5 vs 7 or with xp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-06T17:34:32-07:00","id":1101038,"title":"","content":"Look. Mage Revised. Page 166. Though you are correct, I missed darksight right before it. But Darksight explicitly gives you access to the entire scientific spectra of light. From X-Ray to Electromagnetic, to Thermal or even SOUND.<br /> <br /> I'm coming at this from the perspective of plentiful resources. I'm coming at this from the perspective of &quot;I have prime 4 and maybe forces 3 and Matter 2.&quot; At the bare minimum. More helps, and certainly helps to demonstrate the concept. But in the end, a the system can come online with just this.<br /> <br /> We're talking a starting character who's earned 55 XP. So firmly in the realm of 'midlevel' play. 13 chapters into the game if you're a good player. Possibly sooner, depending on how long your ST does story's rather than chapters. That's what, 3 months of play? If you start at 'base mage with no XP'<br /> <br /> Meanwhile the hermetic has to earn 64 XP just to advance their Arete once and upgrade Spirit from 3-4. Are there ways to build around this? Yes. But those could be used in the industrialist player as well. Sphere Natural for example. Helps our monosphere focused Hermetic more than the Industrial Etherite with their interplay of several spheres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11744,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","user":"Enginseer-42","date":". 06-06-2017, 08:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T10:42:55-07:00","id":1101293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099918-for-a-technomancer-is-there-any-reason-ever-not-to-use-wonder-spheres?p=1100664#post1100664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You build the production facility which is a wonder in it's own right, admittedly requiring some setup time. And then it really is insert tass, push button, get wonder. Again, if you look at the rules for wonder creation and wonder use, this is how they interact. The primary limit is how much tass you can obtain and the actual mundane crafting of the shells. The quickening itself is ludicrously trivial with the aid of wonders.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incidentally, if I had a player create a Prime 4 Wonder to make more Wonders, I'd be sorely tempted to have some spirit from Autochthonia possess it and have it create more identical, self-replicating Wonder-production engines. It would be the craziest grey goo scenario ever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T11:03:34-07:00","id":1101298,"title":"","content":"Such a Device is not a bad idea if you have tons of Quint, and don't want to waste your time making Wonders with your Arete. Of course, it only makes a specific type of Wonder (because it's a single effect that has a <i>System</i>). One Hit-Mark generator can't create anything but Hit-Marks. Perhaps it can't even create other models of Marks but only the one it was designed to create. That's how Artifacts work.<br /> <br /> This is how I assume most Marks are created. It's not like Masters of Matter/Mind/Prime don't have better things to do than to be all day and night rolling Arete to deploy army after army of these toys. They created the first one (A Wonder that does his thing, without the versatility of all of the Spheres limitless potential combined), and then another Wonder that creates them to be used by less brillant minds","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T11:34:34-07:00","id":1101305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1099918-for-a-technomancer-is-there-any-reason-ever-not-to-use-wonder-spheres?p=1101298#post1101298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Such a Device is not a bad idea if you have tons of Quint, and don't want to waste your time making Wonders with your Arete. Of course, it only makes a specific type of Wonder (because it's a single effect that has a <i>System</i>). One Hit-Mark generator can't create anything but Hit-Marks. Perhaps it can't even create other models of Marks but only the one it was designed to create. That's how Artifacts work.<br /> <br /> This is how I assume most Marks are created. It's not like Masters of Matter/Mind/Prime don't have better things to do than to be all day and night rolling Arete to deploy army after army of these toys. They created the first one (A Wonder that does his thing, without the versatility of all of the Spheres limitless potential combined), and then another Wonder that creates them to be used by less brillant minds</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Though like any other device you could modify it to build something else later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}